== verdict
==============================================================================
  !! triplet SA-CASSCF unconverged at r = 1.6391, 1.6891 A

  OFFSET at equilibrium (vertical a 3A" <- X 1A'):
    CASCI      3.3901 eV
    SC-NEVPT2  2.3444 eV   (07, own singlet CASSCF: 3.5502)
    FIC-NEVPT2 3.4961 eV
    references 03 3.4477, 04 3.4142, mean 3.4310 eV
    SC -1.087 eV and FIC +0.065 eV from the reference mean; FIC - SC = +1.152 eV
    -> The contraction accounts for part of it: FIC moves towards the references
       but the remainder has another source.

  SLOPE of the triplet energy over 1.639-1.739 A (band width scales with it):
    SC  -5.681 eV/A    FIC -15.486 eV/A    FIC/SC = 2.726
    (vertical-energy slope: SC -4.119, FIC -6.282 eV/A)
    -> Shapes differ by 172.6%, beyond 3%. A band computed on the SC
       surface would be that much too wide or narrow: the surface itself needs FIC.

  COST per geometry, wall: orbitals 108 s, FIC 3 s (two states), SC 2 s (two states)
  For a raster only the triplet is needed per point, so roughly half of each NEVPT2 figure.
